From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement position: sticky

Ports blitz#887 (by LinuxBoy-96) to this revision. A sticky box is laid out
as relative, with its insets hidden from Taffy; after layout, sticky.rs
resolves each registered box's constraints from its nearest scroller (or the
viewport) and its containing block, and every scroll write and paint
re-applies them as a per-box offset. The offset is applied in paint, hit
testing, hoisted-child positions and the geometry APIs (absolute position,
offsetTop, getBoundingClientRect, and so the accessibility bounds), while
scrollIntoView keeps the in-flow position. In porting: IS_STICKY moved to a
free NodeFlags bit; the offset goes into physical_unrounded_geometry (both
the plain and the writing-mode versions) instead of a second unrounded
position helper; paint applies it in node_transform and refreshes it at the
top of paint_scene_damaged, and paint_bounds uses it so damage records match
what is drawn; the inset override keeps stylo_taffy's writing-mode rect();
a refresh that moves a box bumps the geometry generation; table row
backgrounds and the debug overlay follow shifted cells. Adds
position_sticky tests (stuck and released headers, containing-block end,
bottom insets, hit testing, a sticky thead, a stacked list header, paint).
